@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title One request, one account/project: dual storage context binding
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "auth.py middleware" as Auth
participant "workspace_context()\n<<async context manager>>" as Context
participant "workspace : WorkspaceStore" as Store
participant "dataset.py / coursework_store.py\n<<ContextVar adapters>>" as Adapters
participant "Private route / domain functions" as API
participant "Account SQLite" as DB

activate Auth
note over Auth : Precondition: session, Origin/CSRF and request limits validated.\nUser ID comes from identity, not from the request's project selector.
Auth -> Context : enter workspace_context(user, request)
activate Context
Context -> Store : construct(data_dir, user.id, selected project)\nin thread pool
activate Store
Store -> DB : ensure account tables; require selected project
activate DB
DB --> Store : existing/new account tables and validated project, or error
deactivate DB
Store --> Context : initialized store or safe storage error
deactivate Store
alt Initialization succeeded
  Context -> Adapters : enter dataset.use_storage(store)\nand coursework_store.use_storage(store)
  activate Adapters
  Adapters --> Context : ContextVar tokens bound
  deactivate Adapters
else Invalid account/project or storage failure
  note over Context : Do not dispatch private routes or fall back to global files.
end
Context --> Auth : bound request context or rejection
deactivate Context
opt Valid private context
  Auth -> API : dispatch coursework or dataset operation
  activate API
  API -> Adapters : load/save selected corpus, profile or screenshot
  activate Adapters
  Adapters -> Store : corresponding DatasetStorage / CourseworkStorage method
  activate Store
  Store -> DB : project-qualified read or locked transactional mutation
  activate DB
  note over DB : Mutations bump workspace version; entry changes also record revisions.\nProfile JSON and screenshot base64 remain in this account database.
  DB --> Store : data/commit or database error
  deactivate DB
  Store --> Adapters : value/bytes or safe failure
  deactivate Store
  Adapters --> API : operation result
  deactivate Adapters
  API --> Auth : HTTP response or translated error
  deactivate API
  Auth -> Context : exit workspace context in finally
  activate Context
  Context -> Adapters : reset stored ContextVar tokens
  activate Adapters
  Adapters --> Context : previous contexts restored
  deactivate Adapters
  Context --> Auth : cleanup complete
  deactivate Context
end
deactivate Auth
legend bottom
  Protocol dispatch is structural; no per-user global CSV path is mutated.
  No class association multiplicity is implied by a sequence participant.
  Legacy CSV/profile/screenshot access requires no bound adapter and explicit no-auth maintenance.
  Default web requests require authentication; production refuses require_auth=False.
endlegend
@enduml
